3. Work completed
3.1 ASR parameter tuning
Problem. The production transcription call used chunk_length_s=10. Whisper's encoder is trained exclusively on 30-second windows and HF pads every chunk to 30s regardless, so 10s chunks create a train/inference distribution mismatch. Separately, the three fallback thresholds (compression_ratio_threshold, logprob_threshold, no_speech_threshold) were suspected inert, because a scalar temperature=0.0 never triggers the temperature-fallback loop. Language was also not pinned.
Method. A two-round, human-judged parameter sweep across 15 decoding configurations. No WER, no gold transcripts, no metrics harness — this scope was deliberately cut to keep the cycle short. Transcripts were emitted blind-labelled, aligned across four 60–90 second windows per call (opening, numbers-heavy, difficult, close), and read side by side against a fixed rubric: deletions, degenerate loops, number accuracy, domain-term accuracy, script flipping, phantom text over silence.
Round 1 — six windowing/chunking configurations.
Round 2 — nine further changes stacked on the Round 1 winner: language pinning, n-gram blocking, beam search, temperature ladder, vocabulary priming.
Result.
Round 1 winner: config D — chunk_length_s=30, stride_length_s=3
Round 2 winner: config I — no_repeat_ngram_size=0 (n-gram blocking disabled)
Config N (beam search without n-gram blocking) judged worse than I.
Recommended production configuration: chunk 30s, stride 3s, no n-gram guard, temperature=0.0 scalar, timestamps on, three fallback thresholds retained but understood to be inert in the chunked path.
