6. Working principles adopted
Human judgment is the evaluation signal at ambiguous quality decisions; automated metrics were deliberately deprioritised for ASR.
Never change two things at once. If three prompts move in an afternoon, causality is lost.
Read individual failures, not aggregates. The number says something changed; the calls say what.
When the model and the annotator disagree and the model is right, fix the codebook and re-label — don't patch the prompt.
Scope aggressively. Cut anything that lengthens the cycle without changing the decision.